  "review": {
    "book": "2KI",
    "entityID": "person:amaziah_214",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 12:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "For Jozacar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his servants, struck him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in David’s city; and Amaziah his son reigned in his place."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 13:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, and his might with which he fought against Amaziah king of Judah, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the second year of Joash, son of Joahaz, king of Israel, Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah began to reign."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Amaziah sent messengers to Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, “Come, let’s look one another in the face.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, “The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, ‘Give your daughter to my son as wife.’ Then a wild animal that was in Lebanon passed by, and trampled down the thistle."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Amaziah would not listen. So Jehoash king of Israel went up; and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth Shemesh, which belongs to Judah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at Beth Shemesh and came to Jerusalem, then broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now the rest of the acts of Jehoash which he did, and his might, and how he fought with Amaziah king of Judah, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah lived after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz, king of Israel, fifteen years."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah, aren’t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "All the people of Judah took Azariah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in the place of his father Amaziah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah, Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel began to reign in Samaria for forty-one years."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the twenty-seventh year of Jeroboam king of Israel, Azariah son of Amaziah king of Judah began to reign."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was right in the LORD’s eyes, according to all that his father Amaziah had done."
      }
    ],
